.TH OMACALENDARCTL 1 "2026" "OmaCalendar" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omacalendarctl \- command-line client for the OmaCalendar service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omacalendarctl
.RI [ options ]
.I method
.RI [ json_params " | " \- ]
.br
.B omacalendarctl
.RI [ options ]
.BR today " | " agenda " [" \-\-days
.IR N "] | " add
.IR TEXT " | " sync " | " methods
.br
.B omacalendarctl
.RI [ options ]
.B backup
.RB [ \-\-copy\-to
.IR PATH ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B omacalendarctl
talks to
.BR omacalendard (1),
the OmaCalendar background service, over its user-local socket at
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/omacalendar/daemon.sock .
.PP
In raw mode it sends one IPC method with optional JSON parameters and prints
the response as one line of JSON on standard output. Errors are printed as JSON
on standard error and the exit status is 1. The methods are documented in
.IR /usr/share/doc/OmaCalendar/docs/IPC.md .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B today
List today's events in the display time zone.
.TP
.B agenda
List events from today for
.B \-\-days
days (default 7).
.TP
.BI add " TEXT"
Create an event from quick-add text such as
.IR "Lunch with Sam fri 12:30 @ Cafe" .
Text without a time creates an all-day event. The event goes to the default
calendar unless
.B \-\-calendar
names one.
.TP
.B sync
Sync every account and wait for it to finish (default timeout 120 seconds).
.TP
.B methods
List the IPC methods the running service supports.
.TP
.B backup
Save a consistent copy of the calendar database to
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/omacalendar/backups/calendar\-<UTC time>.sqlite3
with owner-only permissions; the newest 5 backups are kept there. With
.BR \-\-copy\-to ,
also copy it to a file or into a directory. The backup holds calendars, events,
tasks and settings but no passwords or sign-in tokens, which stay in the
keyring; after restoring on another machine, sign in to each account again.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \- ", " \-\-params\-stdin
Read the JSON parameters from standard input. Use this for passwords and
client secrets, which would otherwise be visible to other local users in the
process list and saved in shell history.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
Wait up to SECONDS (1 to 3600) for each response. The default is 5, or 120 for
.B sync
and
.BR backup .
.TP
.B \-\-watch
After the response, keep the connection open and print notifications as JSON
lines on standard output. Use it with
.BR system.subscribe .
Without it, notifications go to standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print a command's result as JSON instead of text.
.TP
.BI \-\-days " N"
Number of days for
.B agenda
(1 to 366).
.TP
.BI \-\-calendar " ID"
Calendar for
.BR add .
.TP
.BI \-\-copy\-to " PATH"
For
.BR backup :
also copy the backup to PATH, or into PATH when it is a directory. An existing
file is never overwritten.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
omacalendarctl today
omacalendarctl agenda \-\-days 14
omacalendarctl add "Dentist tue 9:30 for 45 min"
omacalendarctl backup \-\-copy\-to ~/Backups/
omacalendarctl system.info
omacalendarctl \-\-watch system.subscribe '{"topics":["events"]}'
printf '%s' "$params" | omacalendarctl accounts.addCalDav \-
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any error, including a timeout or an unreachable service.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR omacalendar (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
